    "evidence_text": "state-of-the-art baseline models, including hierarchical ones, to enable fair comparison with the hierarchical MPAD variants.\n\nDoc2vec (or paragraph vector) is an extension of word2vec that learns vectors for documents in a fully unsupervised manner.\n\nDocument embeddings are then fed to a logistic regression classifier.\n\nDAN .\n\nThe Deep Averaging Network passes the unweighted average of the embeddings of the input words through multiple dense layers and a final softmax.\n\nRecursive neural networks are stacked and applied to parse trees.\n\nLSTMN  is an extension of the LSTM model where the memory cell is replaced by a memory network which stores word representations.\n\nSPGK  also models documents as word co-occurrence networks.\n\nWMD  is an application of the well-known Earth Mover's Distance to text.\n\nHere, a CNN is applied to semantic units obtained by clustering words in the embedding space.\n\nsee in Table TABREF29 that having more iterations improves performance.\n\nto better performance, while on Polarity and IMDB, it is the opposite.\n\nRemoving the master node deteriorates performance across all datasets, clearly showing the value of having such a node.",
